#: tt/sync_messages.py:40
msgid "No server address is set. Enter one above and save it first."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:41
msgid ""
"The address must start with https:// - a token sent over plain HTTP could be "
"read by anyone on the way."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:43
msgid "Please enter both a username and a password."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:44
msgid "Wrong username or password."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:45
msgid "Too many sign-in attempts on the server. Try again in a minute."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:48
msgid "The server's certificate could not be verified."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:49
msgid "The server did not answer in time."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:50
msgid "The server could not be reached. Check the address and your connection."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:51
msgid ""
"The address answered, but not like a TimeControl sync server. Check that it "
"points at the right directory."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:53
msgid ""
"This account has used up its storage on the sync server, so new changes are "
"kept on this device until there is room. Nothing is lost. A device that is "
"fully synchronised frees space on its next sync; if none is, the server's "
"limit has to be raised."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:58
msgid ""
"The address redirects somewhere else. Enter the address it points to instead "
"- this device will not follow a redirect, because that could send its access "
"token on to an unencrypted one."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:62
msgid "The server is reachable but has not been set up yet."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:63
msgid ""
"The server was dealing with something else. This one retries on its own."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:66
msgid "This device is not signed in to the server."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:68
msgid ""
"The saved server address is not the one this device is signed in to. Sign in "
"again to start using it."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:71
msgid ""
"End-to-end encryption is switched on for this account, but this device does "
"not have the key yet. Enter the passphrase in the settings."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:74
msgid ""
"The stored key does not belong to these settings - the salt or the account "
"has changed since it was made. Enter the passphrase again in the settings."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:77
msgid ""
"End-to-end encryption is switched on, but the settings carry no salt to "
"derive the key from. Switch it off and on again, or copy the settings from "
"the device that has it."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:81
msgid ""
"The server holds encrypted data, but end-to-end encryption is switched off "
"on this device. Nothing has been changed here. Switch it on and enter the "
"passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:85
msgid ""
"Encrypted data arrived that this device could not read. Nothing has been "
"changed here. Check that the passphrase is the same one the other device "
"uses."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:88
msgid ""
"Data arrived that was sealed with a key this device does not have. Usually "
"that means the passphrase was changed on another device. Enter the new one "
"here as well - nothing has been changed or lost."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:92
msgid "End-to-end encryption is switched off for this account."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:93
msgid ""
"The server says a change came from a different device than the one that "
"actually made it. Nothing has been applied here. If this does not clear up, "
"the server is not doing what it should."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:97
msgid ""
"The server sent a change that had already been received, or sent two of them "
"the wrong way round. Nothing has been applied here. If this does not clear "
"up, the server is not doing what it should."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:103
msgid ""
"This device has to be fully synchronised before the passphrase can be "
"changed, because the change is only complete once the server has accepted a "
"document sealed with the new one. Let it synchronise and try again."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:107
msgid "That is the passphrase this account already uses."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:109
msgid "There is nothing to seal yet. Create a project first."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:111
msgid "The synchronisation files on this computer could not be written."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:112
msgid ""
"The stored copy of the data could not be fetched from the server, so "
"catching up had to stop."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:117 tt/sync_messages.py:120
msgid ""
"This machine tried to send more at once than the server accepts. It will "
"keep trying, but cannot get past this on its own."
msgstr ""

#: tt/sync_messages.py:138
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The server would not accept what this machine sent ({code}). The two are "
"probably running different versions."
msgstr ""

